For quite some time now, I've thought that (yn)holy water has some
logical inconsistencies in relation to the rest of the game. For
example, why are all chaotic players burned by holy water? Including
chaotic priests?
Also, while you can lob a carafe of holy water at a demon or vampire,
the damage it does hardly justifies losing a potion bottle.

So, I made a patch, linked here: http://www.greyfire.org/~l/holy.diff

It actually does a lot of things, such as:

* Making it so that any alignment can quaff holy water.
* Making thrown/wielded (un)holy water do more damage.
* Making thrown/wielded holy water insta-kill non-unique demons.
* Making thrown/wielded unholy water insta-kills angelic beings ('A')
except for Archons.
* Making it so that hitting werecritters with holy water 'cures' them
(changes them into player-monsters.)

And much, much more! (Note: there _is_ more. Check it out.)

